ows\nfor certain squares of the form\n<MATH_0015>\nand some choices of <MATH_0016>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80b0e15705f0ae6a2e4f92b5a433d27527d90a557fffb6fe6941e5cb651ee96c", "unit_id": "tag:0CLF:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CL9", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-cat-dotted-arrows-composition}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:270840aa397a035a5d113beb78036ea020b796c143872d4c405030038aa7fcf6", "source_text": "This lemma is a special case of Categories, \nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b245c87b9067c179e1e5d25006d352d34d5c459f45f3cbaf9dfce6e9876a27d", "unit_id": "tag:0CLF:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0CL9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\gamma$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-diagram}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-fill-in-diagram}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-uniqueness}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6ce2cafa111e23b01128244b4f279dac2888c76df84157a48fde3b3c50059e07", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:76db27cae31a87161ed8c0023a8abaa50f8b7b96b9dd9e7f5b34f643b4d167ca", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nWe say <MATH_0002> satisfies the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>uniqueness part of the valuative criterion<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif for every diagram (<REF_0001>) and <MATH_0003>\nas in Definition <REF_0002>\nthe category of dotted arrows is either empty or\na setoid with exactly one isomorphism class.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a9287edf94ed918015b787769576e216736559072ac5c8c5852015864eae652d", "unit_id": "tag:0CLG:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CL9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-uniqueness}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3ccd8efe924ee0f4df67bfdf202e98073cc10db94bd0c4a011e4d2d889571d03", "source_text": "The base change of a morphism of algebraic stacks which satisfies the\nuniqueness part of the valuative criterion by any morphism of\nalgebraic stacks is a morphism of algebraic stacks which satisfies the\nuniqueness part of the valuative criterion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ca73e63c37898fb5dcbbb06c2f4b7885288f1596e07ac6ee303a47403a30c261", "unit_id": "tag:0CLH:statement"}
